## {{ sections.method }}. Method

### Counts

Every count is exact, over the {{ base.n_rows | num }} rows of the dataset{% if skipped %}, without the columns left out{% endif %}.

- **Missing value:** an empty cell, or a value that could not be read as the number or date
  its column holds{% if unparsed %} (section {{ sections.changes }}){% endif %}.
- **Distinct values:** different values of a column, missing values not counted.
- **Duplicate row:** a row equal in every column to an earlier one. The first of each set of
  copies is not counted, so 3 equal rows are 2 duplicates. Rows are compared through a 64-bit
  hash of their values.

### When each issue is reported

- **Many missing values:** more than {{ settings.high_missing_pct | pct }} % of the values of a column are missing.
- **Duplicate rows:** at least one duplicate row.
- **Constant column:** a column with exactly one distinct value; it may also have missing
  values. A column with no value at all is reported as missing values instead.
- **Possible identifier:** at least {{ identifier.min_distinct_pct | round | int }} % of the values of a column are
  distinct, and they are integers, or text codes with (almost) no spaces such as references
  or emails. The column needs at least {{ identifier.min_rows }} values, except integers whose column name
  says id (`id`, `user_id`, `orderId`). A few repeats are allowed: in a file with duplicate
  rows the ids repeat too. Dates, decimal numbers and free text are not reported, even when
  every value is distinct.
- **Highly correlated columns:** two columns of type numeric whose {{ settings.correlation_method | capitalize }} correlation is
  above {{ settings.high_correlation }} or below -{{ settings.high_correlation }}. Each pair is computed over the rows where both
  columns have a value; infinite values count as missing. Columns of other types
  (identifiers, booleans) and constant columns are not compared.
{% if settings.correlation_columns < settings.numeric_columns %}
  Only {{ settings.correlation_columns }} of the {{ settings.numeric_columns }} numeric columns were compared: those with the
